%S A063736 7,7,3,7,5,7,2,7,7,7,7,3,1,5,7,6,7,7,6,7,3,7,5,7,4,7,7,7,7,3,3,1,7,6,
%T A063736 7,7,6,5,3,7,5,7,2,6,7,7,7,3,7,5,7,6,7,7,7,7,3,7,5,7,4,3,5,7,7,3,7,5,
%U A063736 6,6,7,7,3,5,3,7,5,7,6,7,7,3,7,3,5,4,7,4,7,7,2,7,3,6,5,7,6,7,7,7,7,3,7,5,7
%N A063736 To get a(n), the pattern of the possible squarefree triple (4n+1, 4n+2, 4n+3) is coded as follows: compute A008966(x) getting one of {000, 001, 010, 011, 100, 101, 110, 111} and convert from binary.
%C A063736 All code values arise corresponding to 8 classes of patterns. E.g., the first nonsquarefree triple (000 pattern, code=0) appears at 844, [845, 846, 847], 848 as a middle part of a nonsquarefree 5-tuple. Start values of code=7 triples are listed in A007675.
%C A063736 From _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 15 2026: (Start)
%C A063736 Let c_1 = 1 - 24/Pi^2 + 3 * Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 2/p^2) - Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 3/p^2) =  1 - 24/Pi^2 + 6 * A065474 - 4 * A206256 = 0.002148262596124315486371... , c_2 = 8/Pi^2 - 2 * Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 2/p^2) + Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = A217739 - 4 * A065474 + 4 * A206256 = 0.0219809970049606825706..., c_3 = Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 2/p^2) - Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = 2 * A065474 - 4 * A206256 = 0.143320274255252147821..., and c_4 = Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = 4 * A206256 = 0.501947923623237193337... .
%C A063736 Then, the asymptotic densities of the occurrences of 0, 1, ..., and 7 in this sequence are c_1, c_2, c_2, c_3, c_2, c_3, c_3, and c_4, respectively.
%C A063736 The asymptotic mean of this sequence is 7*c_2 + 14*c_3 + 7*c_4 = 56/Pi^2 = 5.673986283970915200857... . (End)
%H A063736 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A063736/b063736.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A063736 a(n) = 4*A008966(4n+1)+2*A008966(4n+2)+A008966(4n+3).
%e A063736 a(0) = 4*A008966(1)+2*A008966(2)+A008966(3) = 4+2+1 = 7.
%e A063736 a(11) = 4*A008966(45)+2*A008966(46)+A008966(47) = 0+2+1 = 3.
%e A063736 a(12) = 4*A008966(49)+2*A008966(50)+A008966(51) = 0+0+1 = 1.
%e A063736 a(13) = 4*A008966(53)+2*A008966(54)+A008966(55) = 4+0+1 = 5.
%e A063736 a(14) = 4*A008966(57)+2*A008966(58)+A008966(59) = 4+2+1 = 7.
%t A063736 a[n_] := FromDigits[Array[Boole[SquareFreeQ[4*n+#]]&, 3], 2]; Array[a, 105, 0] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 15 2026 *)
%o A063736 (PARI) a(n) = fromdigits(vector(3, i, issquarefree(4*n+i)), 2); \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 15 2026
%Y A063736 Cf. A007675, A008966, A068088, A258332 (positions of 0's), A278554, A370600 (positions of 7's).
%Y A063736 Cf. A065474, A206256, A217739.
